{%- comment -%}
    Renders one cart-level discount, e.g. "NEW15 (<riyal> - 16.50)".

    Accepts: discount - one entry from cart.cart_level_discount_applications.

    The money filter wraps the currency symbol in markup, so a minus written in front of
    the whole string lands before the symbol, reading "- SAR 16.50". The sign belongs
    after the symbol and on the digits instead, reading "SAR - 16.50".

    Rather than pattern-match the symbol's markup, find the bare number inside the money
    string and sign that. money_without_currency formats the same amount with no symbol,
    so it is exactly the numeric run that money embedded - wherever the format happens to
    put it, and whatever markup surrounds it. An earlier version keyed off the literal
    '</span> ' and silently fell through to the old output here, because this store's
    money format emits '</span >' with a space before the bracket.

    This lives in a snippet because the cart page (main-cart.liquid) and the cart drawer
    (halo-side-cart.liquid) both render it. It was inlined in both, and fixing one left
    the other showing the old format.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
    assign discount_amount = discount.total_allocated_amount | money
    assign bare_amount = discount.total_allocated_amount | money_without_currency
    assign signed = false

    if bare_amount != blank and discount_amount contains bare_amount
        assign negative_amount = bare_amount | prepend: '- '
        assign discount_amount = discount_amount | replace_first: bare_amount, negative_amount
        assign signed = true
    endif

    unless signed
        assign discount_amount = discount_amount | prepend: '- '
    endunless
-%}
{%- render 'icon-discount' -%}
{{- discount.title }}&nbsp;({{ discount_amount }})
